key|name|url|evidence
first_champ|Bundesliga: German champions in the Bundesliga|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/faq/10-things-on-the-bundesliga/german-champions-in-the-bundesliga-10554|Cologne won the inaugural 1963/64 Bundesliga under Georg Knopfle; the league started with 16 teams.
records|Bundesliga: Player and club records|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/bundesliga-records-goals-titles-attendances-for-players-and-clubs-10555|Gerd Muller scored 365 career goals; Lewandowski scored 41 in 2020/21; Dieter Muller scored six for Cologne against Bremen in August 1977.
leverkusen24|Bundesliga: Bayer Leverkusen are 2023/24 champions|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/bayer-leverkusen-are-2023-24-bundesliga-champions-26930|Xabi Alonso led Leverkusen to their first Bundesliga title in 2024.
league_faq|Bundesliga: Ten things on the Bundesliga|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/faq/10-things-on-the-bundesliga|Bayern won eleven successive Bundesliga titles from 2012/13 to 2022/23; Gladbach first defended the title in 1970/71.
fastest|Bundesliga: Bellarabi, Volland and fastest goals|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/bellarabi-volland-musiala-the-fastest-goals-in-bundesliga-history-24353|Bellarabi for Leverkusen and Volland for Hoffenheim each scored after nine seconds.
long_goal|Bundesliga: Goals and records|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/bundesliga-records-goals-titles-attendances-for-players-and-clubs-24220|Stoppelkamp scored from 82 metres for Paderborn against Hannover in September 2014.
dortmund_guide|Bundesliga: Borussia Dortmund historical guide|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/borussia-dortmund-bundesliga-club-by-club-historical-guide-klopp-reus-zorc-24117|Dortmund's Yellow Wall is its south terrace; Klopp won the 2011/12 titles and Sammer the 2002 title; Zorc made 463 Bundesliga appearances. Bochum and Schalke played the first Bundesliga match at Westfalenstadion in April 1974.
schalke_guide|Bundesliga: Schalke historical guide|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/fc-schalke-04-bundesliga-club-by-club-historical-guide-24140|Schalke contest the Revierderby with Dortmund; Die Knappen means miners; Neuer developed in its academy.
gladbach_guide|Bundesliga: Borussia Monchengladbach historical guide|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/borussia-monchengladbach-bundesliga-club-by-club-historical-guide-heynckes-netzer-24134|Gladbach are the Foals; Weisweiler built the attacking team. Their 1978 Dortmund win was 12-0. Laumen broke a wooden post against Bremen in 1971; their former ground was Bokelbergstadion.
hamburg_guide|Bundesliga: Hamburger SV historical guide|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/hamburger-sv-bundesliga-club-by-club-historical-guide-keegan-seeler-24135|Hamburg were ever-present until relegation in 2018. Seeler was first league top scorer with 30 goals; a giant right-foot statue honours him outside Volksparkstadion.
bremen_guide|Bundesliga: Werder Bremen historical guide|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/werder-bremen-bundesliga-club-by-club-historical-guide-ozil-pizarro-rehhagel-24116|King Otto Rehhagel won Bremen's 1988/1993 titles; Schaaf won the 2004 double; Ozil scored the 2009 cup final's only goal. Werder means a small river island and Weserstadion is named after the Weser.
lautern_guide|Bundesliga: Kaiserslautern historical guide|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/kaiserslautern-bundesliga-club-by-club-historical-guide-rehhagel-24160|Lautern won the league in 1998 immediately after promotion. Fritz Walter captained Germany in 1954 and the stadium bears his name. Josef Pirrung scored twice in the 1973 7-4 Bayern comeback.
stuttgart_guide|Bundesliga: Stuttgart historical guide|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/vfb-stuttgart-bundesliga-club-by-club-historical-guide-klinsmann-werner-khedira-24118|Kimmich developed at Stuttgart; white shirts have a red hoop. Elber, Bobic and Balakov formed the Magic Triangle; Hildebrand went 884 minutes unbeaten in 2003. Khedira scored the 2007 title clincher. Allgower has 338 Bundesliga appearances and 129 goals for Stuttgart.
freiburg_guide|Bundesliga: Freiburg historical guide|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/freiburg-club-by-club-historical-guide-streich-finke-petersen-24172|Volker Finke led Freiburg's first promotion in 1993 and third-place finish in 1994/95. The body text is used rather than its erroneous 1991-promotion image caption.
bayern_guide|Bundesliga: Bayern Munich historical guide|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/bayern-munich-bundesliga-club-by-club-historical-guide-lewandowski-muller-24115|Bayern won a sextuple under Flick linked to 2019/20; their first Bundesliga game was a 1-0 loss to 1860 in 1965.
frankfurt_guide|Bundesliga: Frankfurt historical guide|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/eintracht-frankfurt-bundesliga-club-by-club-historical-guide-europa-24142|Frankfurt's crest has an eagle; live eagle Attila began flying in 2006. Eintracht means unity; Korbel played 602 Bundesliga matches. Glasner won the 2022 Europa League unbeaten.
mainz_guide|Bundesliga: Mainz historical guide|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/mainz-bundesliga-club-by-club-historical-guide-klopp-tuchel-24188|Klopp led first promotion in 2004; fair play gave 2005/06 UEFA Cup entry. Andersen secured 2009 promotion but was dismissed four days before kickoff; Tuchel succeeded him after winning the U19 national title.
union_guide|Bundesliga: Union Berlin historical guide|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/union-berlin-club-by-club-historical-guide-24212|Fischer led the first Bundesliga promotion in 2019. Fans donated earnings from paid blood donations; rebuilt Alte Forsterei; and have gathered to sing Christmas songs since 2003.
munich1860_guide|Bundesliga: 1860 Munich historical guide|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/1860-munich-club-by-club-historical-guide-bayern-24181|1860 Munich officially opened Allianz Arena against Nuremberg on 30 May 2005.
leverkusen_guide|Bundesliga: Bayer Leverkusen historical guide|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/bayer-leverkusen-club-by-club-historical-guide-havertz-wirtz-ballack-24153|Bayer pharmaceutical workers founded the Factory XI; Kirsten scored 182 club Bundesliga goals. Butt scored 26 league penalties; Hanke lobbed him from kickoff in 2003/04. Ballack's own goal came at Unterhaching on the final day in 2000. Erroneous 2000/01 treble caption and Wirtz academy claim excluded.
hoffenheim_guide|Bundesliga: Hoffenheim historical guide|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/hoffenheim-club-by-club-historical-guide-nagelsmann-hopp-24189|Nagelsmann became youngest permanent Bundesliga coach at 28 in 2016. Rangnick led successive promotions, reaching the Bundesliga in 2008. Hopp co-founded SAP; Compper first represented Germany while at Hoffenheim in November 2008.
leipzig_guide|Bundesliga: RB Leipzig historical guide|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/rb-leipzig-club-by-club-historical-guide-red-bull-24199|Leipzig are the Red Bulls; Red Bull purchased SSV Markranstadt playing rights in 2009. Erroneous Rangnick first-season coach attribution excluded.
augsburg_guide|Bundesliga: Augsburg historical guide|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/augsburg-club-by-club-historical-guide-bavaria-24196|Hain scored the 2011 promotion-clinching goal against FSV Frankfurt. Liverpool ended the first Europa League campaign in the 2016 round of 32. Haller returned in 1973 after winning Italian titles with Bologna and Juventus.
wolfsburg_guide|Bundesliga: Wolfsburg historical guide|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/wolfsburg-club-by-club-historical-guide-volkswagen-de-bruyne-dzeko-magath-24167|Volkswagen staff founded Wolfsburg; Magath coached the 2009 title side with Dzeko and Grafite, the 28-goal top scorer. Mount Magath was a training hill. McClaren became first English Bundesliga coach in 2010.
hertha_guide|Bundesliga: Hertha Berlin historical guide|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/hertha-berlin-bundesliga-club-by-club-historical-guide-24161|Hertha play at Berlin Olympiastadion; their name came from a steamboat and nickname is Old Lady. Dardai holds the Bundesliga appearance record; Boateng brothers debuted professionally at Hertha. Record 88,075 attendance came against Cologne in September 1969.
hannover_guide|Bundesliga: Hannover historical guide|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/hannover-club-by-club-historical-guide-cherundolo-zieler-24165|Cherundolo is Captain America. Hannover scored three own goals against Gladbach in December 2009; Diouf got two yellow cards in 12 minutes in October 2013.
nuremberg_guide|Bundesliga: Nuremberg historical guide|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/nuremberg-club-by-club-historical-guide-gundogan-max-morlock-24164|Nuremberg were relegated in 1969 after winning in 1968; Max Morlock was first German World Cup final scorer and stadium namesake. Fifth-tier Ulm beat Nuremberg 2-1 in the 2001/02 DFB Cup.
beckenbauer|FC Bayern Hall of Fame: Franz Beckenbauer|https://fcbayern.com/en/club/hall-of-fame/franz-beckenbauer|Beckenbauer is known as the Kaiser; after Bayern he played for New York Cosmos and Hamburg.
muller_role|FC Bayern: Thomas Muller farewell interview|https://fcbayern.com/de/news/2025/05/zurueck-ins-funkhaus-thomas-mueller-im-abschieds-interview|Thomas Muller coined Raumdeuter for his style based on space and positioning without the ball.
kahn|FC Bayern Hall of Fame: Oliver Kahn|https://fcbayern.com/en/club/hall-of-fame/oliver-kahn|Kahn is the Titan; he joined from Karlsruher SC in 1994 after 128 Bundesliga appearances there.
robbery|Bundesliga: Bayern's Robbery partnership|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/luis-diaz-michael-olise-have-bayern-munich-got-their-new-robbery-35520|Robbery refers to the Arjen Robben and Franck Ribery partnership.
haaland_debut|Bundesliga: Remembering Haaland's Dortmund debut hat-trick|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/remembering-erling-haaland-debut-hat-trick-borussia-dortmund-augsburg-17469|Haaland came on and scored three in Dortmund's 5-3 Augsburg victory on 18 January 2020. Exact elapsed-time claims excluded because league articles differ.
son|Bundesliga: Son, made in the Bundesliga|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/heung-min-son-tottenham-spurs-leverkusen-hamburg-made-in-bundesliga-3293-2268|South Korea's Son played for Hamburg and Leverkusen before Tottenham.
davies|FC Bayern: Alphonso Davies profile|https://fcbayern.com/en/teams/first-team/alphonso-davies|Davies is a Canadian international; he joined Bayern from Vancouver Whitecaps in January 2019.
podolski|Bundesliga: Retired club shirt numbers|https://www.bundesliga.com/de/bundesliga/news/franz-beckenbauer-lukas-podolski-fc-bayern-munchen-1-fc-koln-trikotnummern-nicht-mehr-vergeben-30058|Lukas Podolski is called Prinz Poldi; Cologne reserved his number 10. Bayern retired Beckenbauer's five in 2024.
okocha|Bundesliga: Okocha's wondergoal against Kahn|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/videos/watch/watch-okocha-s-wondergoal-against-kahn-wIby4JtN|Okocha scored the famous Frankfurt solo goal against Karlsruhe and Kahn in 1993.
raul_schalke|Bundesliga: Raul's move to Schalke in 2010|https://www.bundesliga.com/de/2bundesliga/news/fc-schalke-04-edin-dzeko-weekly-ipp-35797|Raul Gonzalez Blanco moved to Schalke in 2010 after his Real Madrid career.
naldo_derby|Bundesliga: Dortmund-Schalke, matchday 13 in 2017/18|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/matchday/2017-2018/13/borussia-dortmund-vs-fc-schalke-04/liveticker|Schalke trailed 4-0 and drew 4-4; Naldo scored in the fourth minute of stoppage time.
ghost_goals|Bundesliga: Two bizarre ghost goals|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/bizarre-ghost-goals-bayern-munich-bayer-leverkusen-kiessling-24771|Helmer's 1994 ghost goal against Nuremberg led to a replay; Kiessling's 2013 header entered through a hole against Hoffenheim. Goal-line technology began in 2015/16.
frankfurt_attack|Bundesliga: Frankfurt's great attacking tradition|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/hugo-ekitike-omar-marmoush-eintracht-frankfurt-great-strike-partnerships-28778|Jovic, Rebic and Haller formed the Buffalo Herd in 2018/19.
ribery_moments|Bundesliga: Ribery, twelve unforgettable Bayern moments|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/franck-ribery-retires-12-seasons-at-bayern-munich-12-best-moments-1829|Robben and Ribery first shared the pitch for Bayern against Wolfsburg on 29 August 2009 in a 3-0 win.
kane_move|FC Bayern: Harry Kane signed from the Premier League|https://fcbayern.com/de/news/2023/08/wechsel-aus-der-premier-league-fc-bayern-nimmt-harry-kane-unter-vertrag|Kane joined Bayern from Tottenham Hotspur on 12 August 2023.
trophy|Bundesliga: Meisterschale explained|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/title-meisterschale-explainer-champions-bayern-munich-leverkusen-dortmund-32100|The Meisterschale is the champion's shield; Elisabeth Treskow designed it; in 1949 it replaced the lost Viktoria statue.
