streich_exit|Bundesliga: Christian Streich announces departure|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/christian-streich-announces-departure-from-freiburg-after-12-years-as-coach-26621|Streich left Freiburg in 2024 after more than twelve years as head coach; won the DFB Julius Hirsch Honorary Prize in 2023 for combating discrimination.
cottbus_guide|Bundesliga: Energie Cottbus historical guide|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/energie-cottbus-club-by-club-historical-guide-24204|Cottbus fielded the first Bundesliga starting XI with no German players against Wolfsburg in April 2001; reached the 1997 cup final from outside the top two tiers and lost to Stuttgart.
emma|Borussia Dortmund: EMMA glossary|https://www.bvb.de/de/en/borussia-dortmund/glossary/emma.html|EMMA is a bee; the mascot is named after Lothar Emmerich.
karlsruhe_guide|Bundesliga: Karlsruhe historical guide|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/karlsruhe-club-by-club-historical-guide-oliver-kahn-schafer-24171|Winfried Schafer coached Karlsruhe's 1990s European run; Mehmet Scholl developed there; Austria Salzburg eliminated them on away goals in the 1994 UEFA Cup semi-final.
heidenheim_guide|Bundesliga: Heidenheim historical guide|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/1-fc-heidenheim-1846-club-by-club-historical-guide-24332|Frank Schmidt led the club's first Bundesliga promotion in 2023; the Voith Arena is 555 metres above sea level; their first European competition was the Conference League in 2024/25.
stpauli_guide|Bundesliga: St Pauli historical guide|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/st-pauli-club-by-club-historical-guide-hamburg-reeperbahn-kultclub-24198|Hamburg rivals St Pauli play at the Millerntor; skull and crossbones are a fan symbol; the 2003 rescue campaign sold Retter shirts; Football Koalas watched from trees; the club beat Intercontinental champions Bayern in 2002.
fortuna_guide|Bundesliga: Fortuna Dusseldorf historical guide|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/fortuna-dusseldorf-club-by-club-historical-guide-free-tickets-allofs-24168|Klaus and Thomas Allofs starred for Fortuna; the Fortuna For All scheme aims for free home tickets; a bread-factory carriage inspired the name; Gerd Zewe made 440 Bundesliga appearances; Fortuna beat Bayern 7-1 in December 1978.
sane_youth|Bundesliga: Sane's move to Galatasaray|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/leroy-sane-joins-galatasaray-from-bayern-munich-32626|Sane came through at Schalke before Manchester City and Bayern.
bellingham_captain|Bundesliga: Bellingham's captaincy|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/jude-bellingham-borussia-dortmund-captaincy-a-dream-come-true-21408|Bellingham captained Dortmund against Cologne aged 19 on 1 October 2022, the youngest Bundesliga captain since records began in 1995.
bellingham_origin|Bundesliga: Dortmund's talents turned stars|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/bellingham-haaland-lewandowksi-youngsters-turned-stars-dortmund-23792|Bellingham joined from Birmingham City in 2020; Lewandowski joined from Lech Poznan in 2010.
musiala_youth|Bundesliga: Ten things on Musiala|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/jamal-musiala-10-things-on-the-bayern-munich-and-german-midfielder-31124|Musiala represented England's youth teams before choosing Germany in 2021; joined Bayern from Chelsea's academy in 2019. Exclude erroneous age 17 for the 2019 move.
auba_masks|Bundesliga: Aubameyang's spectacular celebrations|https://www.bundesliga.com/de/bundesliga/news/pierre-emerick-aubameyang-sprints-tore-masken-jubel-24375|Aubameyang wore Batman and Spider-Man masks; Reus wore Robin's mask in the 2015 derby celebration.
moukoko_debut|Bundesliga: Youngest league players|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/gio-reyna-moukoko-top-10-youngest-players-in-league-history-9529|Moukoko debuted aged 16 years and one day for Dortmund against Hertha; replaced Haaland. Exclude erroneous calendar date in the article.
pizarro_oldest|Bundesliga: Goal records|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/from-robert-lewandowski-to-gerd-muller-bundesliga-goal-records-24333|Claudio Pizarro became the oldest scorer for Bremen and extended the record in May 2019; do not use conflicting Stoppelkamp distance stated on this page.
lahm_loan|FC Bayern: Lahm's career in pictures|https://fcbayern.com/en/photos/2017/05/gallery-philipp-lahms-career|Lahm went on loan to Stuttgart, established himself under Felix Magath and first wore number 21 there.
makaay_profile|FC Bayern: Roy Makaay legends profile|https://fcbayern.com/en/teams/fc-bayern-legends/players/roy-makaay|Makaay was nicknamed The Phantom; scored Bayern's 3000th Bundesliga goal in August 2006; returned to the Netherlands with Feyenoord in 2007.
format|Bundesliga: League structure FAQ|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/faq/what-are-the-rules-and-regulations-of-soccer/how-is-european-soccer-structured-with-leagues-and-cup-competitions-10568|The Bundesliga has 18 teams and each club plays 34 league games. Exclude outdated Ligue 1 team count.
klinsmann_life|Bundesliga: Ten things on Klinsmann|https://amp.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/jurgen-klinsmann-10-things-on-the-germany-legend-and-hertha-berlin-coach-usmnt-9887|Klinsmann trained as a baker and gained a commercial helicopter pilot licence; played under the alias Jay Goppingen in the United States.
klose_salto|Bundesliga: Miroslav Klose legend|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/miroslav-klose-germany-fifa-world-cup-legend-bayern-munich-lazio-werder-bremen-17848/|Klose was nicknamed Salto Klose for his somersault goal celebration. Do not use potentially erroneous club statistics on this page.
bayer1988|Bundesliga: Leverkusen's historic comeback|https://www.bundesliga.com/en/bundesliga/news/5-reasons-why-bayer-leverkusen-will-progress-against-bayern-munich-champions-league-wirtz-alonso-31137|Leverkusen overcame Espanyol in the 1988 UEFA Cup final; Cha Bum-kun scored the aggregate equaliser and Rudiger Vollborn saved in the shootout.
